---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Service | Vemor Consulting LLC"
  description="Terms of service for Vemor Consulting LLC's services, including Vemor Comps settlement data reports."
  path="/terms"
>
  <section class="hero" style="min-height:0; padding-bottom:40px;">
    <span class="hero-tagline">Legal</span>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--text-muted);">Last updated: August 17, 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:800px;">
      <h2>1. Services</h2>
      <p>
        Vemor Consulting LLC ("Vemor," "we," "us") provides technology consulting,
        AI automation, managed operations, and data report services, including but
        not limited to Vemor Voice, Vemor Comps, Custom Builds, and Managed AI
        Operations (collectively, the "Services").
      </p>

      <h2>2. Vemor Comps Reports</h2>
      <p>
        Vemor Comps reports are licensed to the requesting firm or individual for
        use in their matters and internal analysis. Reports are derived from
        publicly filed documents on the California Department of Industrial
        Relations PAGA Case Search portal and are provided for informational
        purposes only. Reports do not constitute legal advice, and no
        attorney-client relationship is created by ordering, receiving, or using
        a report. Vemor is not a law firm and does not provide legal services.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Data Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        Vemor uses automated extraction, verification, and consistency-checking
        processes to produce reports. While we take commercially reasonable steps
        to ensure accuracy, all data is subject to the accuracy and completeness
        of the underlying public filings. Vemor does not warrant that reports are
        free from error. Users are responsible for independently verifying any
        data used in legal proceedings or professional advice.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        Reports and their presentation, structure, and analysis are the
        intellectual property of Vemor Consulting LLC. The requesting firm
        receives a non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use report content
        in connection with their legal practice. Underlying public-records data
        is not proprietary to Vemor.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Subscriptions and Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Subscription terms, pricing, and billing cycles are established in the
        service agreement between Vemor and the subscribing firm. Subscriptions
        renew automatically unless cancelled in writing before the renewal date.
        Single-report orders are billed upon delivery.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, Vemor's total liability for any
        claim arising from the Services shall not exceed the fees paid by the
        client for the specific report or service giving rise to the claim. Vemor
        shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, consequential, or
        punitive damages, including lost profits or damages arising from reliance
        on report data.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Vemor Consulting LLC, its
        officers, and contractors from any claims, damages, or expenses arising
        from your use of the Services or reports in a manner inconsistent with
        these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Modifications</h2>
      <p>
        Vemor reserves the right to update these terms at any time. Material
        changes will be posted on this page with an updated date. Continued use
        of the Services after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California. Any
        disputes shall be resolved in the courts of San Diego County, California.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms may be directed to
        <a href="mailto:gio@vemor.ai" style="color:var(--gold);">gio@vemor.ai</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
